  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "expanding-glycomics-0644",
  "summary": "New preprints rewrite deepTools, MAUDE and per-base storage for cohort scale, while database updates add precomputed variant and atlas resources.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is re-engineering of existing analysis steps for scale and reuse rather than new analytical paradigms. deepTools4 rewrites core functions with benchmarked speed-ups, MAUDE-Py ports a probabilistic CRISPR-screen framework to Python, pbzarr stores per-base data for thousands of samples in Zarr and is reported faster and smaller than D4 and bigWig, and CyteArc enables out-of-core single-cell analysis beyond 100M cells. Breedbase and CATEomics extend this to integrated breeding workflows and model selection for treatment-effect estimation in omics. A parallel thread is reusable precomputed resources: Evo2VED provides Evo2 variant scores for 6.48M gnomAD variants, the Biodiversity Cell Atlas reprocesses 39 single-cell atlases uniformly, and GI-DB and the CNCB-NGDC update expand population and database coverage. A public genomic-hash dataset for 1000 Genomes individuals also appears.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
